      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7e221134-b417-54a6-9874-9cff476b40ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: A. J. Watson, Rodger Ward\n- Roles: race driver, aviator, car designer\n- Places: Pocono International Raceway, Trenton, Indianapolis, Milwaukee\n- Events: Indianapolis 500, USAC National Championship, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Rodger M. Ward was born on January 10, 1921, and later served as a P-38 aviator in the United States Air Force during World War II.\n- Rodger Ward was an American open-wheel race driver in North America who earned 26 top-level race victories, including two Indianapolis 500 wins and two USAC National Championships.\n- Rodger Ward conceived the classic tri-oval design and layout of Pocono International Raceway, modeling it on his favorite turns at Trenton, Indianapolis, and Milwaukee.\n- A. J. Watson built cars that Rodger Ward drove to 18 race victories.\n- Rodger M. Ward died on July 5, 2004.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
